{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2773 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a1659515b4205d36ee4bc41fa2f245cbc56b28277c2b1b801ca2971ba9366ae4" :edb/db-before-t 2772 :edb/db-after-t 2773 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536085 50 #inst "2026-10-16T01:03:23.258Z" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564844 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564845 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564846 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564849 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564857 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564876 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564900 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1038 #edb/ref 17592186564921 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186172039 1040 #edb/ref 17592186564924 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564848 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564875 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564883 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-9x$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1072 #uuid "02cbb13a-a6d7-5c1c-8f40-eee3ed956640" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564844 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=-9x.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0.$ In each open quadrant, $x$ has a fixed nonzero sign. The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/83/8306880f3f6b3d936d1e690cf75eb9e1a999f5b1c914d10c1886296317664fbe.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant." 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564868 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564904 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564922 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1072 #uuid "0310b6c3-7a71-5e78-8f0c-a9029c12ce0c" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564845 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIn an open quadrant, each squared coordinate is positive, so the remaining coordinate factors and coefficient determine the sign.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ec462e2ce1055ca352de84813bc6d72731d74f93d44a1513b1dc284b504cb0b.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564846 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564850 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564846 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564858 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] 