85 17592186045443 true] [17592186564857 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564857 1072 #uuid "26112629-51c5-582f-837e-44806c4fa45a" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564857 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIn an open quadrant, each squared coordinate is positive, so the remaining coordinate factors and coefficient determine the sign.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ec462e2ce1055ca352de84813bc6d72731d74f93d44a1513b1dc284b504cb0b.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\n