-8bc7-b184038b82c9" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564920 1080 "false" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564920 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564920 1083 #uuid "ef4a105b-ceb3-5369-a285-0eb8ccce9659" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564852 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564877 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564897 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=5{x}^{2}y$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **III.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1072 #uuid "f3c5f9ee-c923-5bed-81c7-8afd53970e0b" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564921 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}y.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIn an open quadrant, each squared coordinate is positive, so the remaining coordinate factors and coefficient determine the sign.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/b1/b151d959cb74133709e15f9a78b377988609bf761c174ca82f15fcf1d8d3d74c.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564915 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564922 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564920 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564922 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564922 1077 "II" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564922 1078 #edb/ref 17592186564920 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564922 1079 #uuid "f521ac1c-ccfd-5b5e-851c-0d50cbcbf7a4" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564890 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186564916 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564923 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564923 1077 "I" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564923 1078 #edb/ref 17592186564890 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564923 1079 #uuid "f5cc4f7c-0e04-5c8b-8cc7-2f7da8f3de2a" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564924 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186172039.py" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true] [17592186564924 1169 #uuid "73579c81-0627-5a43-bb65-b41f57c0ebaf" 13194139536085 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"02cbb13a-a6d7-5c